Alerting:
	goal of alerting is not to detect every anomaly — it’s to reliably detect
	build alerting primarily around user-facing SLIs and SLOs rather than raw infrastructure metrics alone.
	Define SLIs for latency, error rate, availability per service
	Set SLOs like 99.5% of requests succeeded over 30 days


Common SLIs:
	Availability / Success rate
		successful_requests / total_requests
		SLO: 99.9% of requests succeed over 30 days
	Latency
		p50/p95/p99
		SLO: 95% of requests complete in < 200ms
	Error rate
		5xx_responses / total_requests
		SLO: Error rate stays below 0.1%
		alert 30 day budget gone in 2 days, alert
	Throughput / Traffic
		requests/sec
		bytes/sec
		jobs/sec
		queue throughput	
		SLO: System sustains 50k requests/sec without degradation
	Saturation
		CPU utilization
		memory pressure
		queue depth
		thread pool exhaustion
		DB connection pool exhaustion	
		SLO: CPU utilization remains under 80% for 99% of intervals
	Durability
		Objects not lost / total stored objects
		SLO: 99.999999999% yearly durability Correctness
	Freshness / Staleness
		SLO: 95% of events appear in search within 60 seconds
	
Google’s “Four Golden Signals”
Latency:	How long requests take
Traffic:	Demand on system
Errors:		Failed requests
Saturation:	Resource exhaustion

